cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite the article and identify the commit used."
type: software
title: "Nonhalting and PA-independence for a 213-state Turing machine"
authors:
  - family-names: "Chang"
    given-names: "James"
repository-code: "https://github.com/jamesyc/BusyBeaver"
abstract: >-
  Assuming the consistency of ordinary Peano arithmetic, an explicit binary
  Turing machine with 213 working states runs forever on a blank tape and PA
  cannot prove its nonhalting sentence. Since the natural numbers model PA,
  PA cannot refute that sentence either. The Lean formalization checks the
  machine simulation, the internal implication from nonhalting to PA
  consistency, and the two-sided independence corollary.
